The resolver now rejects storing a function with read effects in a multi-dimensional array element, and storing one as the result of a method call in a field, an array element or a yield parameter of an iterator (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/483). The check that prevents a function from reading itself looked only at assignments into a field or a one-dimensional array element, so `m[0, 0] := f`, or `r[0] := Id(f)` for a method `Id` that returns its argument, could tie a knot and prove `false`. For a call, the check looks at the type of the out-parameter, with the call's type arguments. The hidden option `--legacy-function-store-locations` restores the old, unsound check, for migration and comparison only.
